sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Administrator / Moderator
    participant P1 as Web Application (Moderation UI)
    participant P2 as CommentModerationController
    participant P3 as ModerationDecisionService
    participant P4 as Application Database
    P0->>P1: open comment review queue
    P1->>P2: GET /admin/comments (filters)
    P2->>P4: query pending comments, reports, flags and history
    P4-->>P2: return paginated review data
    P2-->>P1: render admin/comments
    P1-->>P0: display review queue and revision
    P0->>P1: choose allow / hide, enter reason
    P1->>P2: POST /admin/comments/{id}/decision
    P2->>P2: validate action, reason, optional expected_revision
    P2->>P3: decide(actor, id, action, reason, expectedRevision)
    P3->>P3: authorize verified admin/moderator
    P3->>P4: begin transaction, lock comment, read open reports/flags
    P4-->>P3: return current status and revision
    alt [revision mismatch or invalid transition]
    P3-->>P2: 409 conflict, transaction rolls back
    P2-->>P1: return conflict response
    P1-->>P0: ask reviewer to reload current comment
    else [valid decision]
    P3->>P4: allow → published, hide → hidden, increment revision
    P3->>P4: insert moderation history with actor/action/reason
    P3->>P4: resolve open reports and flags, commit
    P4-->>P3: return history ID
    P3-->>P2: decision saved
    P2-->>P1: JSON: confirmation
    P1-->>P0: refresh review queue / show saved decision
    end
    Note over P0,P4: content_type=shorts routes to ShortCommentDecisionService and short-video tables. No AI re-evaluation or new legacy feedback/assessment record is created by this decision.
